 that tariff free and  delay free so that is what I hope we  will be achieving in the negotiations  which are going on now let me say tariff  free and delay free yes because if you  listen to what the government is saying  at the minute it feels as if sovereignty  the opportunity try diverge and  sovereignty over rules regulations laws  is being prioritized above the  frictionless trade that you described as  so I think the government Act you  understand this extremely well all I  will say we've had lots of really  significant ministers have around the  table particularly Michael Gove coming  up spending time with the automotive  industry I convened a round table for  him to come and discuss and I am very  confident that he understands as does  the Prime Minister exactly what is at  stake here so my role as the leader  representative of the West Midlands will  be to continue to make that case and I'm  actually determined we do come through  on this I mean they also say that they  will accept checks if necessary yes they  and that means delays and the big it  well that we wait to say about that  actually there are ways that this come  in a bear in mind a lot of product that  comes in to supply chains from outside  the EU already has checks and there are  not delays actually so I'm up for the  negotiation and it's quite right at the  beginning of this what are we now ten  months of negotiation that we've put  this is a really clear requirement on  the table and it's have the debate of  course so running for re-election to be  where Mary  West Midlands that election in May are  you looking forward Hank Boris Johnson  on your leaflets we've done a leaflet  across the region this sent last month  and his face is on the leaflet alongside  me because it's a very important point  my job is to encourage the prime  minister and all of his team to take the  decisions for the West Midlands  unfortunately I wish it wasn't like this  the big financial decisions are still  all taken in London I would true  devolution we would be taking more of  them ourselves but at the moment they're  taking London so my job is to lobby for  that investment and that's exactly why  I'm very proud to say I work with the  Prime Minister on taking those decisions  hs2 a very good example this week if you  had to sum up the pitch in a couple  sentences what would you say and the  pitches I think straight forward that  the West Midlands was an area that  perhaps didn't achieve all its potential  for 40 years we were perhaps the worst  performing area of the country but over  the last three years we've really  bounced back dramatically you've seen it  in jobs in housing in transport  investment so don't change but it's now  proving to win for our people
 

